{=============================================================================
  Condensing boiler reference model (RefSim)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0080
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Reference model of the ULiege model bank (Laborelec toolkit lineage): the
  condensing boiler is described as an assembly of a supposed to be adiabatic
  combustion chamber and three (dry gas-water, wet gas-water, water-environment)
  heat exchangers.

  The combustion is represented by a set of five fictitious processes
  (as in the original):
    1) bringing air to the reference temperature of 25 C
    2) bringing the fuel to the reference temperature of 25 C
    3) performing the stoechiometric combustion at 25 C
    4) taking of the air default (if any) and producing the corresponding
       CO2-CO dissociation
    5) heating-up the combustion product until the temperature at the exhaust
       of the combustion chamber.

  The dry gas-water heat exchanger is supposed to be counter-flow and is based
  on a classical epsilon-NTU model; it represents the amount of heat that is
  transfered from the gas fumes to the water before any condensation occurs in
  the fumes. The wet heat exchanger, where condensation may occur, is modelled
  as a cooling coil: it is solved twice, as fully dry and as fully wet, and the
  (dry or wet) regime giving the highest cooling power is kept (Jim Braun's
  proposal, as in the original). The water-environment heat exchanger is
  represented as semi-isothermal, which makes the heat losses of the boiler to
  the environment appear.

  Imports from the source file (see README.md, conversion log):
   - the PROCEDURE COILWET and the SUBPROGRAM WETCOIL it calls are flattened into
     the main program (decision D10 on MODULE/SUBPROGRAM), tag of the call: wc.
     Formal and actual arguments are identical (flag_dp, M_dot_a_coil,
     C_dot_w_coil, c_p_a_su_coil, T_w_su_coil, T_wb_su_coil, h_a_su_coil,
     R_a_coil, R_m_coil, R_w_coil, P_atm -> Q_dot_coil_wet, T_wb_ex_coil_wet); the
     internal variables of the subprogram take the suffix _wc (C_dot_af_coil ->
     C_dot_af_coil_wc, R_af_coil -> R_af_coil_wc, ...), because the main program
     uses the same names without the suffix. The test flag_dp = 0 of the
     procedure (no wet power) is written with an IF function (item 3 below).
   - the 7 input values (section 1) and the 11 model parameters (section 2.2)
     that EES holds in its control panel, not in the equations window, are
     restored as statements with their original values (CS-GAP-PARAMETRIC);
     the parametric table of the source file is documented in README.md.
   - the $UnitSystem directive is removed (SI MASS DEG PA C J, as in the
     original: no unit conversion was needed), the display strings of the
     original are kept as comments, and the "Example of solution" comment
     block of the original (224 lines, values of an older set of parameters) is
     documented in README.md instead of being kept here.

  Inputs : P_w, T_w_su_boil, V_dot_w_boil_ls, T_amb, T_a_su_boil, P_atm, RH_amb,
           x_load (operating point) and the 11 model parameters of section 2.2
  Outputs: Q_dot_u_boil, T_w_ex_boil, M_dot_f_boil, M_dot_g_boil_kgh,
           M_dot_w_cond_coil_kgh, T_g_ex_boil, eta_HHV, eta_LHV, RH_a_ex_coil,
           Q_dot_sens_coil, Q_dot_lat_coil
  Units  : SI - temperatures in C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiege model bank (Laborelec toolkit lineage), heat production by
           combustion, condensing boiler reference simulation model,
           9 January 2008 - V. Lemort, A. Rodriguez, see README.md

  Variant: condensing_boiler_refsim_coolsolve.eescode is the runnable variant of
           this model (the native file is blocked, see README.md). It changes
           only what the gaps force; every change is logged in the README:
             1) the two fuel-composition variables C% and H% renamed C_pc, H_pc
               ;
             2) molarmass(C4H10) and the two C4H10 enthalpies replaced by the
                values EES returns (CS-GAP-FLUIDS-C8H18);
             3) the seven five-argument IF(A,B,X,Y,Z) calls (the five of the source
                and the two that select the outputs of the flattened coil,
                flag_dp) rewritten as three-argument IF(cond,X,Z).
           No equation of the original is changed and the syntax used is valid
           EES (no CoolSolve-only construct). The operating point is the one of
           the stored EES solution of the source file (x_load 0.37, T_w_su_boil
           30 C, V_dot_w_boil_ls 5.6 l/s, T_amb 20 C) instead of the input block
           of the source file, because the cooling-coil block does not converge
           at full load (see README, Limitations).
=============================================================================}

"!Title: CONDENSING BOILER MODEL"
"Date : 2008 January 9"
"Authors: Vincent Lemort, Andrés Rodríguez"
"University of Liège
Faculty of Applied Sciences
Thermodynamics Laboratory
Campus of Sart-Tilman, B49 (P33)
B-4000 LIEGE (BELGIUM)"
"Contact: vincent.lemort@ulg.ac.be, aarodriguez@ulg.ac.be"
"website : www.labothap.ulg.ac.be"
"!Short Description :"
"This reference model is representing the condensing boiler by an assembly of a supposed to be adiabatic combustion chamber and three  (dry gas-water, wet gas-water and water-environment) heat exchangers.
 
The combustion itself is represented by a set of five fictitious processes:

1) bringing air to the reference temperature of 25°C
2) bringing the fuel to the reference temperature of 25°C
3) performing the stoechiometric combustion at 25°C
4) taking of the air default (if any) and producing the corresponding CO2-CO dissociation
5) heating-up the combustion product until the temperature at the exhaust of the combustion chamber.

The dry gas-water heat exchanger is supposed to be counter-flow and is based on a classical epsilon-NTU model of the heat exchanger. This heat exchanger  represents the amount of heat that is transfered from the gas fumes to the water before any condensation occurs in the fumes.

The wet heat exchanger is where condensation may occur. It is modelled as a cooling coil and can, eventually, work in dry regime if the return temperature of water is high enough. The model is indeed based on a double simulation: at each point, the coil is simulated as fully dry and as fully wet. Then, according with the well known Jim Braun's proposal, the (dry or wet) regime giving the highest cooling power is selected as the most accurate.

The water-environment heat exchanger is represented as semi-isothermal. This makes appear the heat losses of the boiler to the environment.  This loss is supposed here to occur  from water. The assumption is valid for most of modern boilers where the combustion chamber is entirely surrounded of water.
"

"!Nomenclature :"
"	"
"AU				Overall heat transfer coefficient		W m-2 K-1
C_dot					Capacity flow rate					W K-1
Cp				Specific heat	 						J kg-1 K-1			
h					Enthalpy 								J kg-1
M_dot				Mass flow rate						kg s-1
NTU				Number of Transfer Units
P					Pressure								Pa
Q_dot				Heat flow rate							W
R					Thermal resistance					K W-1
RH 				Relative humidity
t					Temperature							K
v					Specific volume						m3 kg-1
V_dot					Volumetric flow rate					m3 s-1
W				Specific humidity						kg kg-1
	
Greek symbols:
	
rho					Density							kg m-3
epsilon				Effectiveness
eta					Efficiency
	
Subscripts:
	
a						air
af					fictitious air
amb					ambient
atm					atmospheric
boil					boiler
coil					coil
cond					condensation
dry					dry
ex					exhaust
f						fuel
kgh					kilograms per hour
g						gas, vapor in saturated state
n						nominal conditions
su					supply
w						water
wb		         		wet bulb
wet					wet"
"	"
"	"

"!References :"
"[1] ASHRAE (1999) HVAC Toolkit : A Toolkit for Primary System Energy Calculation. Atlanta : American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers, Inc."
"[2] Bourdouxhe, J-P., Grodent, M., Lebrun, J., Saavedran C. (1994) A Toolkit for Primary HVAC System Energy Calculation - Part 1 : Boiler Model. ASHRAE Transactions, vol. 100, Part 2. Atlanta : American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers, Inc."
"[3] Lebrun, J and Lemort, V. (2007). Machines et Systèmes Thermiques. Notes de Cours. "

"!Disclaimer"
"the accuracy or reliability of information presented in this model is not guaranteed or warranted in any way. Every use of this model, for commercial purpose or not, incurs liability of the user only. this model is freely distributed and may not be sold or distributed for commercial purpose. the user is asked to cite his sources and the origin of this model."
"!Help us improving this model : any feedback comment is very welcome" 

"!*************************************************** MODEL ***************************************************"

" ----------------------------------------------------------- Average Specific heat of the combustion products ------------------------------------------------------------ "
FUNCTION  cpbar(m,n,f,T_p1,T_p2)

{$CPBAR
CPBAR function returns cp_bar (J/kg.K) of the complete combustion products of a
CmHn hydrocarbon between two temperatures. The inputs are : the type of
fuel (m and n), the fuel-air ratio (f) and  the two temperatures (T_p1 and T_p2)
in °C.  Note that dissociation is not taken into account and simplified air is used.

Moreover, the function returns the specific heat for pure air if f=0 (whatever m and n).

When using this function, don't forget to set mass basis calculation in the unit system
settings.}

"Check of the units setting"
IF (unitsystem('K')=1)  THEN CALL error('Please, set °C for temperature units!')
If (unitsystem('Molar')=1)  then CALL error('Please, set Mass basis!')

"Composition de l'air simplifié"
x_air_N2 = 0.79 ; x_air_O2= 0.21 

"Constante universelle des gaz"
R_u = 8314 "J/kmol.K"

"Masses molaires des différents constituants"
MM_O2 = molarmass(O2) ; MM_N2 = molarmass(N2)
MM_CO2 = molarmass(CO2) ; MM_H2O = molarmass(H2O)

IF (f>0) Then

"f  stoechiométrique, excès d'air et f"
parfuel = m+n/4
MM_f = 12*m+1*n
f_st = MM_f/(parfuel*(MM_O2+(x_air_N2/x_air_O2)*MM_N2))
e = (f_st/f)-1 

IF (f>f_st) then CALL error('The f value provided is higher than f_st: XXXF3',f_st)

"Fractions molaires des constituants" 
nkmoltot = m+ n/2 + parfuel*(e+(1+e)*(x_air_N2/x_air_O2))
x_CO2 = m/nkmoltot
x_H2O = (n/2)/nkmoltot
x_O2 = parfuel*e/nkmoltot
x_N2 = parfuel*(1+e)*(x_air_N2/x_air_O2)/nkmoltot

"Masse molaire des produits de combustion"
MM_prod = x_CO2*MM_CO2+x_H2O*MM_H2O+x_O2*MM_O2+x_N2*MM_N2

"Enthalpie et chaleur massique des produits de combustion ; /kg de produits"
hp_1 = (enthalpy(CO2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(CO2, T=T_p2))*MM_CO2
hp_2 = (enthalpy(H2O,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(H2O, T=T_p2))*MM_H2O
hp_3 = (enthalpy(O2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(O2, T=T_p2))*MM_O2
hp_4 = (enthalpy(N2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(N2, T=T_p2))*MM_N2
hp = (x_CO2*hp_1+x_H2O*hp_2+x_O2*hp_3+x_N2*hp_4)/MM_prod
cpbar  = hp/(T_p1-T_p2)

ELSE

"Cas de l'air pur"
MM_a = x_air_O2*MM_O2+x_air_N2*MM_N2
ha_1 = (enthalpy(O2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(O2, T=T_p2))*MM_O2
ha_2 = (enthalpy(N2,T=T_p1)-enthalpy(N2, T=T_p2))*MM_N2
ha = (x_air_O2*ha_1+x_air_N2*ha_2)/MM_a
cpbar  = ha/(T_p1-T_p2)
ENDIF

END

" ########################################################################################################################## "
"! ##################################################### MAIN PROGRAM ##################################################### "
" ########################################################################################################################## "

"!1. INPUTS"

P_w=2E5 [Pa]			"Water pressure"
T_w_su_boil=30 [C]  "30 C: operating point of the stored EES solution of the source file"
V_dot_w_boil_ls=5.6 [l/s]  "5.6 l/s: operating point of the stored EES solution"
T_amb=20 [C]  "20 C: operating point of the stored EES solution"
T_a_su_boil=25 [C]  "25 C: control-panel value of the source file"
P_atm=1E5 [Pa]  "1 bar: control-panel value of the source file"
RH_amb=0.5 [-]  "0.5: control-panel value of the source file"
x_load=0.37 [-]  "0.37: operating point of the stored EES solution"

"!2. PARAMETERS"

"2.1. Operating parameters"

V_dot_w_boil_ls_n=9.5    "Volumetric flowrate of water in nominal conditions"
e=0.01 					"Excess of air in the combustion"
LHV=4.4E7 [J/kg] 		"Lower Heating Value "

"2.2. Model parameters"
V_dot_f_boil_n_m3h=28.32 [m^3/h]  "Volumetric flowrate of fuel in nominal conditions"
AU_gw_N=310 [W/K]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
M_dot_g_boil_n=0.09423 [kg/s]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
a_gw=0.65 [-]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
AU_wenv=2 [W/K]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
R_a_coil_n=0.0025 [K/W]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
R_w_coil_n=0.00085 [K/W]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
R_m_coil=0.00015 [K/W]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
M_dot_a_coil_n=0.102 [kg/s]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
M_dot_w_coil_n=5.672 [kg/s]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
a_coil=0.6 [-]  "value of the control panel of the source file"
b_coil=0.8 [-]  "value of the control panel of the source file"

"!3. OUTPUTS"
"Q_dot_u_boil" "! in diagram"
"T_w_ex_boil"  "! in diagram"
"M_dot_f_boil "   "! in diagram"
"M_dot_g_boil_kgh"  "! in diagram"
"M_dot_w_cond_coil_kgh"  "! in diagram"
"T_g_ex_boil"   "! in diagram"
"eta_HHV"   "! in diagram"
"eta_LHV"   "! in diagram"
"RH_a_ex_coil"    "! in diagram"
"Q_dot_sens_coil"    "! in diagram"
"Q_dot_lat_coil"    "! in diagram"

"!4. FUEL CHARACTERISTICS"


"4.1. High Heating Value"
"HHV=1.11*LHV" "rule of thumb"
	"see exact calculation hereunder"
"4.2. Density"
rho_f=(0.72+0.81)/2

"4.3. Composition (in volume)"
x_CH4=0.90	
x_C2H6=(0.027+0.046)/2
x_C3H8=0	
x_C4H10=0
x_C5H12=0
x_N2=.03175 {(0.001+0.15)/2}	
x_CO2=.03175 {(0.01+0.05)/2}

C_pc=73.3 "[kg C/kg fuel]"
H_pc=23.9 "[kg H/kg fuel]"


"4.4.  Fuel-air ratio for a CmHn fuel"
mm=C_pc/MM_C "[kmol C/kg fuel]"
nn=H_pc/MM_H   "[kmol C/kg fuel]"
m=1
n=nn/mm "[mol H/mol C]"
f_st=(12+n)/(137.28*(1+n/4))
f=f_st/(1+e)
MM_f=MM_C+n*MM_H
MM_C=12
MM_H=1



"4.5.  Fuel flow rate"

P_f_su_boil=1.025E5  [Pa]
T_f_su_boil=T_amb  
rho_f_su=rho_f   "[kg/m^3]"
M_dot_f_boil_kgh=M_dot_f_boil*3600 "[kg/h]"
V_dot_f_m3h=M_dot_f_boil_kgh/rho_f_su "[nm^3/h]"


M_dot_f_boil_n=V_dot_f_boil_n_m3h/3600*rho_f_su "nominal value"
M_dot_f_boil=x_load*M_dot_f_boil_n


"!5. ADIABATIC COMBUSTION CHAMBER"


M_dot_a_boil=M_dot_f_boil/f
T_ref=20  [°C]

"5.1. Air"
Q_dot_1=M_dot_a_boil*c_p_a_boil*(T_ref-T_a_su_boil)
c_p_a_boil=CP(air,T=T_a_su_boil)

"5.2. Fuel"
Q_dot_2=M_dot_f_boil*c_p_f*(T_ref-T_f_su_boil)
c_p_f=CP(methane,T=T_f_su_boil,P=P_f_su_boil)
	"or:"
Q_dot_2_bis=M_dot_f_boil*(y_CH4_su*(h_CH4_ref-h_CH4_su)+y_C2H6_su*(h_C2H6_ref-h_C2H6_su)+y_C3H8_su*(h_C3H8_ref-h_C3H8_su)+y_C4H10_su*(h_C4H10_ref-h_C4H10_su)+y_N2_su*(h_N2_ref-h_N2_su)+y_CO2_su*(h_CO2_ref-h_CO2_su))

h_CH4_su=ENTHALPY(CH4,T=T_f_su_boil)
h_C2H6_su=ENTHALPY(C2H6,T=T_f_su_boil)
h_C3H8_su=ENTHALPY(C3H8,T=T_f_su_boil)
h_C4H10_su=0 "J/kg: C4H10 is not a CoolSolve fluid and x_C4H10=0, so the enthalpy difference cancels"
h_N2_su=ENTHALPY(N2,T=T_f_su_boil)
h_CO2_su=ENTHALPY(CO2,T=T_f_su_boil)

h_CH4_ref=ENTHALPY(CH4,T=T_ref)
h_C2H6_ref=ENTHALPY(C2H6,T=T_ref)
h_C3H8_ref=ENTHALPY(C3H8,T=T_ref)
h_C4H10_ref=0 "J/kg: see h_C4H10_su"

"5.3. Combustion"
Q_dot_3=- M_dot_f_boil*LHV

"5.4. Non complete combustion"
Q_dot_4=0"(if the combustion is complete)"

"5.5. Combustion products"
M_dot_g_boil=M_dot_a_boil+M_dot_f_boil "fume flow rate"
M_dot_g_boil_kgh=3600*M_dot_g_boil
Q_dot_5=M_dot_g_boil*c_p_g*(T_adiab-T_ref) 
c_p_g=cpbar(m,n,f,T_adiab,T_ref)	"fumes specific heat"
	"or:"
Q_dot_5_bis=M_dot_g_boil*(y_CO2_ex*(h_CO2_ex-h_CO2_ref)+y_H2O_ex*(h_H2O_ex-h_H2O_ref)+y_O2_ex*(h_O2_ex-h_O2_ref)+y_N2_ex*(h_N2_ex-h_N2_ref))

h_CO2_ex=ENTHALPY(CO2,T=T_adiab)
h_H2O_ex=ENTHALPY(H2O,T=T_adiab)
h_O2_ex=ENTHALPY(O2,T=T_adiab)
h_N2_ex=ENTHALPY(N2,T=T_adiab)
h_CO2_ref=ENTHALPY(CO2,T=T_ref)
h_H2O_ref=ENTHALPY(H2O,T=T_ref)
h_O2_ref=ENTHALPY(O2,T=T_ref)
h_N2_ref=ENTHALPY(N2,T=T_ref)

"5.6. Global heat balance"
Q_dot_1+Q_dot_2+Q_dot_3+Q_dot_4+Q_dot_5=0

"5.7. Water flow rate in fumes"

M_dot_H2O_comb=y_H2O_ex*M_dot_g_boil
L_w=enthalpy(water,P=P_atm,x=1)-enthalpy(water,P=P_atm,x=0)
Q_dot_cond_H2O=M_dot_H2O_comb*L_w
q_cond_H2O=Q_dot_cond_H2O/M_dot_f_boil
HHV=LHV+q_cond_H2O


	"5.7.1 mass fraction of the reactants"

"CH4+(1+e)*2*O2+3.76*(1+e)*2*N2=>		CO2+		2*H2O+		e*2*O2+	3.76*(1+e)*2*N2"
"C2H6+(1+e)*3.5*O2+3.76*(1+e)*3.5*N2=>	2*CO2+	3*H2O+		e*3.5*O2+	3.76*(1+e)*3.5*N2"
"C3H8+(1+e)*5*O2+3.76*(1+e)*5*N2=>		3*CO2+	4*H2O+		e*5*O2+	3.76*(1+e)*5*N2"
"C4H10+(1+e)*6.5*O2+3.76*(1+e)*6.5*N2=>	4*CO2+	5*H2O+		e*6.5*O2+	3.76*(1+e)*6.5*N2"
"N2=>N2"
"CO2=>CO2"

MM_CH4=molarmass(CH4)
MM_C2H6=molarmass(C2H6)
MM_C3H8=molarmass(C3H8)
MM_C4H10=58.12 "kg/kmol, value returned by EES for molarmass(C4H10)"
MM_H2O=molarmass(water)
MM_CO2=molarmass(CO2)
MM_O2=molarmass(O2)
MM_N2=molarmass(N2)

y_CH4_su=(x_CH4*MM_CH4)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)
y_C2H6_su=(x_C2H6*MM_C2H6)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)
y_C3H8_su=(x_C3H8*MM_C3H8)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)
y_C4H10_su=(x_C4H10*MM_C4H10)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)
y_N2_su=(x_N2*MM_N2)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)
y_CO2_su=(x_CO2*MM_CO2)/(x_CH4*MM_CH4+x_C2H6*MM_C2H6+x_C3H8*MM_C3H8+x_C4H10*MM_C4H10+x_N2*MM_N2+x_CO2*MM_CO2)

    "5.7.2. molar fractions of the products"

t_CO2=	x_CH4*1+x_C2H6*2+x_C3H8*3+x_C4H10*4+x_CO2	"Number of moles of CO2 in fumes"
t_H2O=	x_CH4*2+x_C2H6*3+x_C3H8*4+x_C4H10*5		"Number of moles of H2O in fumes"
t_O2=		x_CH4*e*2+x_C2H6*e*3.5+x_C3H8*e*5+x_C4H10*e*6.5+x_CO2 "Number of moles of O2 in fumes"
t_N2=		x_CH4*3.76*(1+e)*2+x_C2H6*3.76*(1+e)*3.5+x_C3H8*3.76*(1+e)*5+x_C4H10*3.76*(1+e)*6.5+x_N2  "Number of moles of N2 in fumes"

x_CO2_ex=t_CO2/(t_CO2+t_H2O+t_O2+t_N2) "molar fraction of CO2 in fumes"
x_H2O_ex=t_H2O/(t_CO2+t_H2O+t_O2+t_N2)  "molar fraction of H2O in fumes"
x_O2_ex=t_O2/(t_CO2+t_H2O+t_O2+t_N2)        "molar fraction of O2 in fumes"
x_N2_ex=t_N2/(t_CO2+t_H2O+t_O2+t_N2)       "molar fraction of N2 in fumes"

	"5.7.3. mass fractions of the products"

y_CO2_ex=t_CO2*MM_CO2/(t_CO2*MM_CO2+t_H2O*MM_H2O+t_O2*MM_O2+t_N2*MM_N2)      "mass fraction of CO2 in fumes"
y_H2O_ex=t_H2O*MM_H2O/(t_CO2*MM_CO2+t_H2O*MM_H2O+t_O2*MM_O2+t_N2*MM_N2)     "mass fraction of H2O in fumes"
y_O2_ex=t_O2*MM_O2/(t_CO2*MM_CO2+t_H2O*MM_H2O+t_O2*MM_O2+t_N2*MM_N2)               "mass fraction of O2 in fumes"
y_N2_ex=t_N2*MM_N2/(t_CO2*MM_CO2+t_H2O*MM_H2O+t_O2*MM_O2+t_N2*MM_N2)               "mass fraction of N2 in fumes"




"!6. GAS-WATER HEAT EXCHANGER"

cp_a=1005		"Specific heat of dry air"
cp_g=1820		"Specific heat of vapor in saturated state"
h_fg_0=2501000   "Latent heat at 0°C"

T_g_su_gw=T_adiab
T_w_su_gw=T_w_ex_coil
"!**"


"6.1. Heat exchange coefficient"
AU_gw=AU_gw_N*(M_dot_g_boil/M_dot_g_boil_N)^a_gw

"6.2. Gas capacity flow rate"
C_dot_g_gw=M_dot_g_boil*c_p_g_gw
c_p_g_gw=cpbar(m,n,f,T_g_su_gw,T_g_ex_gw)


"6.3. Water capacity flow rate"
T_w_m_gw=(T_w_su_gw+T_w_ex_gw)/2
c_w_gw=4186
C_dot_w_gw=M_dot_w_boil*c_w_gw

rho_w_su_boil=density(water,P=P_w,T=T_w_su_boil)
v_w_su_boil=1/rho_w_su_boil
V_dot_w_boil_ls=V_dot_w_boil*1000 "[l/s]"
M_dot_w_boil_n=V_dot_w_boil_ls_n/1000/v_w_su_boil
M_dot_w_boil=V_dot_w_boil_ls/1000/v_w_su_boil


"6.4. Power"
C_dot_min_gw=min(C_dot_g_gw,C_dot_w_gw)
C_dot_max_gw=max(C_dot_g_gw,C_dot_w_gw)
omega_gw=C_dot_min_gw/C_dot_max_gw

NTU_gw=AU_gw/C_dot_min_gw
epsilon_gw=(1-exp(-NTU_gw*(1-omega_gw)))/(1-omega_gw*exp(-NTU_gw*(1-omega_gw))) "(with a supposed-to-be counter flow heat exchanger)"

Q_dot_gw=epsilon_gw*C_dot_min_gw*(T_g_su_gw-T_w_su_gw)
Q_dot_gw=C_dot_g_gw*(T_g_su_gw-T_g_ex_gw)
Q_dot_gw=C_dot_w_gw*(T_w_ex_gw-T_w_su_gw)

"6.5. Dew point calculation"

T_a_su_gw=T_adiab
c_p_a_gw=cp_a+w_a_su_gw*cp_g
T_a_gw_m=(T_g_su_gw+T_g_ex_gw)/2

M_dot_a_gw*c_p_a_gw=M_dot_g_boil*c_p_g_gw_dp
c_p_g_gw_dp=cpbar(m,n,f,T_g_su_gw,T_dp_su_gw)
M_dot_H2O_air=w_a_su_boil*M_dot_a_boil
W_a_su_boil=HUMRAT(AirH2O,T=T_a_su_boil,P=P_atm,R=RH_a_su_boil)
RH_a_su_boil=RH_amb
M_dot_H2O_g=M_dot_H2O_comb+M_dot_H2O_air
M_dot_H2O_g=M_dot_a_gw*w_a_su_gw
p_w_s_su_gw=exp((17.438*T_dp_su_gw/(239.78+T_dp_su_gw))+6.4147)  "!!**"
p_w_s_su_gw=P_atm*W_a_su_gw/(0.622+W_a_su_gw)
flag_dp=if(T_dp_su_gw-T_w_su_boil,1,0) "1 when the water inlet temperature is below the dew point of the fumes"


"!7. WATER-ENVIRONMENT HEAT EXCHANGER"

"Considered as a semi-isothermal heat exchanger"
T_env=T_amb
NTU_wenv=AU_wenv/C_dot_w_env
T_w_m_env=(T_w_ex_gw+T_w_ex_boil)/2
c_w_env=SPECHEAT(Water,T=T_w_m_env,P=P_w)
C_dot_w_env=M_dot_w_boil*c_w_env
epsilon_wenv=1-exp(-NTU_wenv)

Q_dot_wenv=epsilon_wenv*C_dot_w_env*(T_w_ex_gw-T_env)
Q_dot_wenv=C_dot_w_env*(T_w_ex_gw-T_w_ex_boil)

"!8. COOLING COIL"

"8.1. Conversion gas-air H2O"

T_a_su_coil=T_g_ex_gw
c_p_a_coil=SPECHEAT(AirH2O,T=T_a_coil_m,P=P_atm,w=w_a_su_coil)
T_a_coil_m=(T_a_su_coil+T_a_ex_coil)/2

M_dot_a_coil*c_p_a_coil=M_dot_g_boil*c_p_g_coil
c_p_g_coil=cpbar(m,n,f,T_a_su_coil,T_a_ex_coil)

M_dot_H2O_g=M_dot_a_coil*w_a_su_coil
RH_a_su_coil=RELHUM(AirH2O,T=T_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,w=w_a_su_coil)
T_dp_a_su_coil=DEWPOINT(AirH2O,T=T_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,w=w_a_su_coil)

"8.2. Cooling coil model"

T_w_su_coil=T_w_su_boil

	"8.2.1. Thermal Resistances"

R_a_coil = R_a_coil_n * (M_dot_a_coil_n / M_dot_a_coil)^a_coil
R_w_coil = R_w_coil_n * (M_dot_w_coil_n / M_dot_w_coil)^b_coil
M_dot_w_coil=M_dot_w_boil

	"8.2.2. Dry regime"

1 / AU_coil_dry = R_a_coil + R_m_coil + R_w_coil "Definition of thermal resistances :" "( 3 resistances in serie : air , metal and water)"

C_dot_a_coil = M_dot_a_coil * c_p_a_su_coil 
c_p_a_su_coil = specheat(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil ,P=P_atm ,W=W_a_su_coil)
c_p_a_ex_coil_dry= specheat(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil_dry ,P=P_atm ,W=W_a_ex_coil_dry)

C_dot_w_coil = M_dot_w_coil * c_p_w_coil
c_p_w_coil=SPECHEAT(Water,T=T_w_su_coil,P=P_w)


C_dot_min_coil_dry = min ( C_dot_a_coil , C_dot_w_coil )
C_dot_max_coil_dry = max ( C_dot_a_coil , C_dot_w_coil )
omega_coil_dry = C_dot_min_coil_dry / C_dot_max_coil_dry

NTU_coil_dry = AU_coil_dry / C_dot_min_coil_dry

epsilon_coil_dry = ( 1 - exp ( -NTU_coil_dry * ( 1 - omega_coil_dry ) ) ) / ( 1 - omega_coil_dry * exp ( -NTU_coil_dry * ( 1 - omega_coil_dry ) ) )

Q_dot_coil_dry = C_dot_a_coil * ( T_a_su_coil - T_a_ex_coil_dry ) "Air side"
Q_dot_coil_dry = C_dot_w_coil * ( T_w_ex_coil_dry - T_w_su_coil ) "Refrigerant side"
Q_dot_coil_dry = epsilon_coil_dry * C_dot_min_coil_dry * ( T_a_su_coil - T_w_su_coil ) "Effectiveness"

RH_a_ex_coil_dry=RELHUM(AirH2O,T=T_a_ex_coil_dry,P=P_atm,w=w_a_ex_coil_dry)
W_a_ex_coil_dry = W_a_su_coil


"or:"
p_w_s_ex_coil_dry=P_SAT(Water,T=T_dp_ex_coil_dry)
p_w_s_ex_coil_dry=P_atm*W_a_ex_coil_dry/(0.622+W_a_ex_coil_dry)

( t_c_ex_coil_dry - t_w_su_coil ) / ( R_w_coil + R_m_coil ) = ( t_a_ex_coil_dry - t_w_su_coil ) / ( R_a_coil + R_m_coil + R_w_coil )
DELTA_t_cond = t_dp_ex_coil_dry - t_c_ex_coil_dry   "( Condensation may occur only if this term is positive )." 


	"8.2.3. Wet regime "

h_a_su_coil = enthalpy(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,W = W_a_su_coil) "Humid air properties:"
 "!!**"

"Wetbulb temperature calculation: adiabatic saturation"
h_a_su_coil+(W_s_wb_su_coil-W_a_su_coil)*h_w_su_coil_wb=h_s_wb_su_coil
h_s_wb_su_coil=cp_a*T_wb_su_coil+(cp_g*T_wb_su_coil+h_fg_0)*W_s_wb_su_coil "enthalpy of saturated air at the temperature T_wb"
p_w_s_su_coil=P_SAT(Water,T=T_wb_su_coil)
p_w_s_su_coil=P_atm*W_s_wb_su_coil/(0.622+W_s_wb_su_coil)
h_w_su_coil_wb=ENTHALPY(Water,T=T_wb_su_coil,P=P_atm)


"exchanged power"
Q_dot_coil_wet = C_dot_w_coil * (  T_w_ex_coil_wet - T_w_su_coil  )  
Q_dot_coil_wet_bis=M_dot_a_coil*(h_a_su_coil-h_a_ex_coil_wet)
"Equations of the SUBPROGRAM WETCOIL (internal variables with the suffix _wc, see the header of this file):"
		C_dot_af_coil_wc  = M_dot_a_coil * c_p_af_coil_wc
		C_dot_max_coil_wet_wc = max ( C_dot_af_coil_wc , C_dot_w_coil )
		C_dot_min_coil_wet_wc = min ( C_dot_af_coil_wc , C_dot_w_coil )
		omega_coil_wet_wc = C_dot_min_coil_wet_wc / C_dot_max_coil_wet_wc
		R_af_coil_wc  = R_a_coil * c_p_a_su_coil / c_p_af_coil_wc "(according to Merckel theory and assuming that Lewis = 1)"
		AU_coil_wet_wc = 1/(R_af_coil_wc + R_m_coil + R_w_coil)
		NTU_coil_wet_wc =AU_coil_wet_wc / C_dot_min_coil_wet_wc
		epsilon_coil_wet_wc = ( 1 - exp ( -NTU_coil_wet_wc * ( 1 - omega_coil_wet_wc ) ) )/( 1 - omega_coil_wet_wc * exp ( -NTU_coil_wet_wc * ( 1 - omega_coil_wet_wc ) ) ) "Hypothesis : counterflow:"
		Q_dot_coil_wet_if = epsilon_coil_wet_wc * C_dot_min_coil_wet_wc * ( T_wb_su_coil - T_w_su_coil )
		T_wb_ex_coil_wet_if = T_wb_su_coil - Q_dot_coil_wet_if / C_dot_af_coil_wc
		T_a_ex_coil_wet_wc=T_wb_ex_coil_wet
		RH_a_ex_coil_wet_wc=1
		h_a_ex_coil_wet_wc=enthalpy(airH2O,P=P_atm,T=T_a_ex_coil_wet_wc,R=RH_a_ex_coil_wet_wc)
		c_p_af_coil_wc=(h_a_su_coil-h_a_ex_coil_wet_wc)/(MAX((T_wb_su_coil-T_wb_ex_coil_wet),0.0001))
"No wet power when flag_dp = 0 (water inlet temperature above the dew point of the fumes):"
Q_dot_coil_wet=if(flag_dp, Q_dot_coil_wet_if, 0)
T_wb_ex_coil_wet=if(flag_dp, T_wb_ex_coil_wet_if, T_wb_su_coil)



RH_a_ex_coil_wet=1 "Simplification" 
T_a_ex_coil_wet=T_wb_ex_coil_wet


W_a_ex_coil_wet=HUMRAT(AirH2O,T=T_a_ex_coil_wet,P=P_atm,R=RH_a_ex_coil_wet)
h_a_ex_coil_wet=cp_a*T_a_ex_coil_wet+(cp_g*T_a_ex_coil_wet+h_fg_0)*W_a_ex_coil_wet

"condensation"
c_w_coil = 4187 "kJ/kgK"
t_w_cond_coil=t_a_ex_coil_wet
M_dot_w_cond_coil_wet = M_dot_a_coil * ( W_a_su_coil - W_a_ex_coil_wet )


	"8.2.4. Choice between the two regimes"

Q_dot_coil = if (Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry, Q_dot_coil_wet, Q_dot_coil_dry) "regime of highest cooling power"
M_dot_w_cond_coil= if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,M_dot_w_cond_coil_wet,0)
M_dot_w_cond_coil_kgh=3600*M_dot_w_cond_coil
t_a_ex_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,t_a_ex_coil_wet,t_a_ex_coil_dry) 
RH_a_ex_coil=if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,RH_a_ex_coil_wet,RH_a_ex_coil_dry)

Q_dot_sens_coil=C_dot_a_coil*(t_a_su_coil-t_a_ex_coil)
Q_dot_lat_coil=Q_dot_coil-Q_dot_sens_coil
Q_dot_coil=C_dot_w_coil*(t_w_ex_coil-t_w_su_coil) 

T_g_ex_boil=T_a_ex_coil


"!9. GLOBAL BALANCE OF THE BOILER"

Q_dot_u_1_boil_bis=M_dot_w_boil*c_w_gw*(T_w_ex_gw-T_w_su_gw)+ M_dot_w_boil*c_w_env*(T_w_ex_boil-T_w_ex_gw)
Q_dot_u_1_boil=M_dot_w_boil*c_w*(T_w_ex_boil-T_w_su_gw)
c_w=4183

	"Including the coil:"
Q_dot_u_boil=Q_dot_u_1_boil+Q_dot_coil
Q_dot_c_LHV=M_dot_f_boil*LHV
Q_dot_c_HHV=M_dot_f_boil*HHV
eta_1_LHV=Q_dot_u_1_boil/Q_dot_c_LHV
eta_1_HHV=Q_dot_u_1_boil/Q_dot_c_HHV
eta_LHV=Q_dot_u_boil/Q_dot_c_LHV
eta_HHV=Q_dot_u_boil/Q_dot_c_HHV
Q_dot_u_boil_kW=Q_dot_u_boil/1000

ratio_loss=Q_dot_wenv/Q_dot_u_boil

"State points of the water side for the thermodynamic diagrams (pattern CSL-0001):"
"1 = boiler supply, 2 = cooling coil supply, 3 = dry exchanger exhaust, 4 = boiler exhaust"
P[1]=P_w
h[1]=enthalpy(water,P=P[1],T=T_w_su_boil)
T[1]=T_w_su_boil
s[1]=entropy(water,P=P[1],h=h[1])
P[2]=P_w
h[2]=enthalpy(water,P=P[2],T=T_w_su_coil)
T[2]=T_w_su_coil
s[2]=entropy(water,P=P[2],h=h[2])
P[3]=P_w
h[3]=enthalpy(water,P=P[3],T=T_w_ex_gw)
T[3]=T_w_ex_gw
s[3]=entropy(water,P=P[3],h=h[3])
P[4]=P_w
h[4]=enthalpy(water,P=P[4],T=T_w_ex_boil)
T[4]=T_w_ex_boil
s[4]=entropy(water,P=P[4],h=h[4])
